Name: MoLE cryptographic stack (sigma-proofs, ihat-rs, anonymous-credit-tokens, mole-core)
Short Name: mole
URL: https://github.com/SamuelSchlesinger/sigma-proofs
URL: https://github.com/Moderation-of-unLinkable-Endorsements/ihat-rs
URL: https://github.com/SamuelSchlesinger/anonymous-credit-tokens
URL: https://github.com/Moderation-of-unLinkable-Endorsements/instantiation
Version: N/A
License: Apache-2.0, MIT
License File: sigma-proofs/LICENSE-APACHE, ihat-rs/LICENSE-APACHE, anonymous-credit-tokens/LICENSE
Security Critical: no
Shipped: no

Description:
The cryptographic implementations behind the MoLE (Moderation of unLinkable
Endorsements) architecture demo:

  * sigma-proofs: sigma protocols and Fiat-Shamir NIZKs (the `act-protocol-id`
    branch, which lets ACT set the Fiat-Shamir protocol identifier its
    specification mandates).
  * ihat-rs: IHAT, pairing-free issuer-hiding anonymous tokens over NIST
    P-256; the MoLE endorsement protocol (type 0x0002).
  * anonymous-credit-tokens: ACT, an anonymous credit scheme over
    ristretto255; the MoLE credential protocol (type 0x0001).
  * mole-core: shared protocol machinery from the MoLE instantiation — the
    TLS-presentation-language wire encoding, the `Mole` HTTP authentication
    scheme, and the directory configuration formats. Vendored so the
    in-browser client is byte-compatible with the mole-anchor /
    mole-moderator servers.

Local Modifications:
Only `src/`, `Cargo.toml`, licenses, and READMEs are vendored (no benches,
examples, or workspace siblings). anonymous-credit-tokens carries the
`sigma-features-trim` branch change restricting sigma-proofs to its
ristretto255 backend.

This is experimental, unaudited cryptography vendored for a local
demonstration. Not for production use.
